-- title:
--   Ordinary twin datum at p with the same Hecke map
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p \neq 2$ and a level $N \geq 1$, a finite set $S$ of naturals, a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$ (adically complete for its maximal ideal) of characteristic zero with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal, a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the weight-$2$ level-$N$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and a noetherian complete local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$ which is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, with local structure map. Assume $p \mid N$ but $p^2 \nmid N$, and that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$. Let $H$ be a datum [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N S 𝒪 θ T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8): a ring map $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ reducing to $\theta$ modulo the maximal ideals, with $\mathcal{O}$-algebra generated by its image equal to $T$, such that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued Hecke character lifting $\theta$ factors through an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map out of $T$, with residue map on $\mathcal{O}$ surjective onto the residue field of $T$, together with an adically continuous rank-two representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Assume further that this residual representation, viewed as an adic representation over the residue field of $T$, is ordinary at $p$, i.e. for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $P$ there is a line spanned by a member of a two-element basis which is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and modulo which inertia at $P$ acts trivially. Then there exists a datum $H'$ for the same data with $H'.\pi = H.\pi$ whose representation $H'.\rho$ is itself ordinary at $p$ in that sense.
--
--   This is the ordinariness, at a prime exactly dividing the level, of the Galois representation carried by a Hecke-algebra datum, in the form of replacing the given datum by one with the same Hecke structure map whose representation is ordinary; classically this is the statement that the $\lambda$-adic representations attached to ordinary weight-two forms are ordinary at $p$, in the families form of Hida and Wiles. It is used by [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset) and by the unit-root computation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_forall_point_apply_eq_unitRoot_of_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_forall_point_apply_eq_unitRoot_of_isOrdinaryAt).
